From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] commands: highlight plain output

Output without colors of its own was one grey text: an error line in a
long log, an address or a value had to be found by reading every line.

The output window gets the switch "Highlight" (on by default, kept in
the browser). For lines that have no terminal colors of their own:

- a line with an error or a warning is tinted red or yellow. The level
  the line states wins over its words: zz1-like logs ([ERR], [WARN],
  [INFO]), syslog (daemon.err, kern.warn, user.info), "ERROR:" or
  "WARNING:" at the start. Otherwise words decide: error, failed,
  denied, unreachable, timed out, not found, invalid, ..., and their
  Russian forms. "0 errors", "no errors", "warnings: 0", "ignoring
  errors", JSON keys ("error": null) and key=value names (error_log=)
  do not make a line an error;
- the buttons "Errors: N" and "Warnings: N" count such lines on the
  screen and scroll to the next one, outlining it;
- error, warning and OK words, IPv4, IPv6 and MAC addresses, URLs,
  sizes, rates, durations, percents, dates and times, quoted strings
  and the key of key=value / "Key: value" / "key": get colors.

Lines with colors of their own are left as they are. The text itself
and "Copy" do not change; "Save" now writes the output without terminal
escape codes too, as "Copy" does (before, a colored output was saved
with them). Lines longer than 2000 characters are not split. Every chunk of output is now a block of its own, so the
browser lays out only the new chunk: without it 20000 highlighted lines
took 6 s instead of 0.7 s to show.

Requires: 003-run-and-settings-pages 004-russian-translation

Checked in Chromium with luci-base 25.12, themes bootstrap and
proton2025 (light and dark), 1280 and 390 pixels wide: zz1 log,
logread, uci show, ip addr, ping, ubus JSON, output with its own
colors, false positives and 20000 lines (1.6 MB): counts, jumps,
switch off and on, no horizontal scroll, same height of the output as
without highlighting, selection copies the same text. The classifier
on 3800 lines of real zz1 logs marks only real errors and warnings;
400 crafted lines of 2000 characters take 0.1 s.
